target: skills/review/review-loop/runlog.py
verify: bash skills/review/review-loop/runlog.test.sh
expect: FAIL  a waived gate does not force partial
why:    one tuple was answering two questions. A waiver PASSES the measurement gate (references/measurement-gate.md:65) so it must not force `partial`, but three runs waiving the same gate is exactly the signal the alarm exists to raise, so it must not go quiet either. Collapsing GATE_ACCOUNTED back onto GATE_OK laundered nothing but downgraded every waived run; collapsing the other way would have made `waived` in review-stats.DECLINED_STATES dead code and hidden a repeated waiver completely. This entry guards the tier half; the review-stats suite guards the visibility half.
--- old
GATE_ACCOUNTED = GATE_OK + ("waived",)
--- new
GATE_ACCOUNTED = GATE_OK
